      8.039999961853027,
      14.039999961853027
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      94.46,
      256.96,
      533.73,
      349.85
    ],
    "text": "Financial Assistance of USD 200 Million from the Asian Development Bank (ADB) for the implementation of the Trade, Investment and Industry Development Program- Sub Program 1 The Government of Sri Lanka had discussions with the Asian Development Bank (ADB) to mobilize a loan amounting to USD 200 million for the Implementation of the Trade, Investment and Industry Development Program- Sub Program 1 under the Policy Based Lending (PBL) facility.",
    "fonts": [
      "Arial Narrow",
      "Arial Narrow,Bold",
      "Trebuchet MS"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      6.0,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      94.46,
      352.03,
      533.67,
      405.29
    ],
    "text": "The program aligned with Sri Lanka\u2019s National Policy Framework, 2025, which aims to build a resilient, inclusive, and sustainable economy. Further, Trade and investment are core government priorities, reflected in the Major Public Investment Projects, 2026\u20132028.",
    "fonts": [
      "Arial Narrow"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      6.0,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      94.46,
      407.47,
      533.59,
      476.47
    ],
    "text": "Accordingly, the Trade, Investment and Industry Development Program was designed to address Sri Lanka\u2019s key development challenges through a programmatic approach. It consists of two subprograms: Subprogram 1, with financing of USD 200 million, and Subprogram 2, with indicative financing of USD 100 million, which is expected to be implemented in 2028.",
    "fonts": [
      "Arial Narrow"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      6.0,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      94.46,
      478.65,
      533.8,
      586.39
    ],
    "text": "Amid heightened economic uncertainty arising from the ongoing Middle East crisis and climate-related shocks, the policy-based loan provides timely and essential support to the Government of Sri Lanka through general budgetary assistance. In this context, ADB agreed to provide an additional USD 100 million in supplementary financing under the Trade, Investment, and Industry Development Program \u2013 Subprogram 1. This increases the initially agreed loan amount from USD 100 million to USD 200 million in total financing.",
    "fonts": [
      "Arial Narrow"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      6.0,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      94.46,
      589.89,
      533.29,
      627.31
    ],
    "text": "The Ministry of Finance, Planning and Economic Development serves as the Executing Agency for the program.",
    "fonts": [
      "Arial Narrow"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      6.0,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      94.46,
      629.49,
      533.78,
      714.46
    ],
    "text": "The loan Agreement was signed on 18 August, 2026 between the Government of Sri Lanka and the Asian Development Bank at the General Treasury in Colombo by Dr. Harshana Suriyapperuma, Secretary, Ministry of Finance, Planning and Economic Development, on behalf of the Government of Sri Lanka and Ms. Shannon Cowlin, Country Director, ADB Sri Lanka Residence Mission, on behalf of the Asian Development Bank.",
    "fonts": [
      "Arial Narrow"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      6.0,
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      94.46,
      716.55,
      349.37,
      761.98
    ],
    "text": "Ministry of Finance, Planning and Economic Development 18 August 2026",
    "fonts": [
      "Arial Narrow"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
